 or assessment of the ILD lesions._________________________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 840, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Talk of naturally occurring molecule, gene, or characteristic by which a particular\npathological or physiological process, disease, etc. can be\nidentified._______________________________\n4.Common features of the disease._________________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 921, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Production of the protein in response to damage to cell__________________\nSSc more commonly occurs with the ILD.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1172, "answer": {"text": ".C", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 7, "prompt": "A more common form of interstitial lung disease_____________________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1290, "answer": {"text": ".B", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "What are known to be more sensitive to change?________________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1507, "answer": {"text": ".thalidomide", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What is known to be closely related to SSc-ILD?______________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1582, "answer": {"text": ".somatic mutation", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Which is an important serum marker for interstitial lung\ndisease? __________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": ".phlebotomy requirement decreases", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "What are the major characteristics of UIP? _______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 90, "answer": {"text": "Myelosuppression", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What is known to play a major role with respect to lung immune host defense? -\n_________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 154, "answer": {"text": ".Endogenous erythroid colony", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "What can be considered a perfect monitoring tool of SSc-ILD\nactivity? ____________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 256, "answer": {"text": ".Erythropoietin (EPO)", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "Which lipoprotein complex plays an essential role in reducing surface tension at the\nair-liquid interface of the lung?\nAnswer ___________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 352, "answer": {"text": ".phlebotomy", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": ".As per HRCT, it can be easy to analyze the extent of the ___________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 849, "answer": {"text": "Myeloid Progenitor", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "The sensitivities in detecting CT-positive ILD was _____________ SP-D.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 923, "answer": {"text": "Endogenous Erythroid Colonies (eec)", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": ".The surfactant may include__________ and hydrophilic proteins.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 999, "answer": {"text": ".Hematopoietic", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": ".There are four major methods for clinical detection of", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1067, "answer": {"text": "Erythropoietin", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "3db4db41e089f915-p5", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "3db4db41e089f915e0031ca1f74179aa0460618f8348cfb44919875c8069d09a", "pages": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "What does this notice explain?\nA Effects of obesity.\nB Effects of weight loss.\nC How weight loss is correlated to other diseases", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 208, "answer": {"text": "Statistics showing the curtailment ratio of the affected people.", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "What is correct about MCP?\nA MCP-1 may play an important role in the development of pulmonary fibrosis in SSc.\nB The abnormal accumulation of macrophages will lead to the production of MCP-1\nC There is not much evidence to show that ILD is directly interlinked to collagen.CCL2\nis known as monocyte c\nhemoattractant protein-1 (MCP-1). MCP-1 is a member of the C-C chemokines. In vivo\nstudies suggest that MCP-1 recruits monocytes/ macrophages to sites of inflammation in\na wide variety of pathological conditions, including ILD. The plasma level of CCL2 is\ncorrelated with FVC value in SSc. However, there was no correlation between ILD\nseverity and primary fibrotic genes such as collagen. That might be because skin fibrosis\npeaks early during the course of SSc and improves later, while fibrosis in pulmonary\ntissue continues to progress even at later stages of disease. A study examined serum\nlevels, spontaneous production by peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC), and\nhistological distribution in the affected skin, of MCP-1. Elevated serum levels of MCP-1\nsignificantly correlated with the presence of pulmonary fibrosis. MCP-1 was expressed in\nmononuclear cells or vascular endothelial cells in 41% (9/22) of SSc patients. The\nfrequency of infiltrating mononuclear cells and endothelial cells that produced MCP-1\nwas significantly higher in SSc patients with early onset than in SSc patients with late\nonset.", "sourcePage": 8, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "Higher among people who are 20+ years.", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "3db4db41e089f915-p11", "label": "Part C · READING 1.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "3db4db41e089f915e0031ca1f74179aa0460618f8348cfb44919875c8069d09a", "pages": [11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16], "questions": [{"number": 9, "prompt": "Which one of these activities are related to automatism?\nA Fumbling\nB Lip smacking\nC Speaking leisurely\nD None", "sourcePage": 13, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 347, "answer": {"text": ".Annual cases of anaplasmosis in the US.", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "Which type of seizure occurs in childhood and may persist into adulthood?\nA Grand mal seizures\nB Petit mal seizures\nC Both A and B\nD None", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": ".Ticks are present throughout the US", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "Which seizures arise from a focally abnormal part of the brain?\nA Petit mal seizures\nB Grand mal seizures\nC Secondarily generalized seizures\nD Both B and C", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 147, "answer": {"text": ".Immune-compromised individuals", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "As per the given information, who may undergo surgery?\nA Patients with grand mal seizures\nB Patients with secondarily generalized seizures\nC Patients with primarily generalized tonic-clonic seizures\nD Both B and C", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 311, "answer": {"text": ".Blood transfusion and organ transplant risks associated with anaplasma species", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "Which one of the following statements correctly describes tonic seizures?\nA Rhythmic jerking\nB Stiffening of muscles\nC Loss of consciousness\nD None", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 533, "answer": {"text": ".Why tests for anaplasmosis appear negative", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "Which one of the following statements is correct?\nA. Infection caused by Fasciola spreads faster than any other types of infections\nB Infection by Fasciola is deadly\nC Infection by Fasciola is treatable\nD Infection by Fasciola is very common", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1796, "answer": {"text": ".All of the above", "source": {"id": "offline-6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d5", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 2.pdf", "sha256": "6a80424d4e2bd5bd51d52aa94ba5d1a7b84e1c23022ba4572374960886802bc7", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-libra